$$
\frac{\partial s}{\partial z}=s(1-s).
$$

The atomic graph stores four local derivatives. Their product is the same quantity:

$$
\underbrace{\left(-\frac{1}{d^2}\right)}_{s=1/d}
\underbrace{(1)}_{d=1+q}
\underbrace{(q)}_{q=\exp(n)}
\underbrace{(-1)}_{n=-z}
=\frac{q}{d^2}=s(1-s).
$$
